# cmd/ccc/TODO
#
# Known codegen gaps and the workarounds still standing in for them in the
# tree.

# shift by a register: c1 used to emit nothing for "x << r", silently
# leaving x unshifted.  The kernel works around it by masking the count so
# the value leaves the register c1 cannot shift by:
#
#	sys/miopic.c	1 << (a & 3)
#	sys/pic.c	1 << (lineir[a] & 7)
#
# The BC case was fixed 2026-10-17 (c1: a shift count in BC builds code,
# and a spill over nothing fails).  With that c1 these shapes all emit a
# real loop now:
#
#	1 << i		add hl,hl loop
#	1 << a[i]	add hl,hl loop
#	x << i		add hl,hl loop
#	(long)x << i	call qshl
#	x >> i		sra h / rr l loop
#
# So the & 3 / & 7 masks are dead workaround unless an IX/IY allocation
# still trips the no-op.  Confirm no such case remains, then drop the
# masks and their comments.
